      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Circuit QED made superconducting circuits a controllable platform for fundamental light-matter physics and quantum information, with broad influence across experimental quantum physics.",
        "attribution": "Blais developed the key theoretical proposal; Wallraff and Schoelkopf led landmark experiments that established and extended the platform. The field is collaborative, so credit beyond these central contributions deserves careful review.",
        "maturity": "The core principles have been replicated across laboratories and underpin a sustained body of experiments and devices.",
