        "Artur K. Ekert",
        "Charles H. Bennett",
        "Gilles Brassard"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Quantum key distribution established an important operational use of quantum measurement and entanglement, with lasting influence on quantum information science.",
        "attribution": "Bennett and Brassard introduced the landmark prepare-and-measure protocol; Ekert developed an entanglement-based approach tied directly to Bell tests.",
        "maturity": "The protocols are theoretically mature and experimentally demonstrated, with practical systems deployed, though security depends on implementation details and threat models.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discovery combines protocol families whose conceptual and experimental histories differ."
        ]
      }
